## 1. Definitions

1.1. "Software" means the GDSS software, source code, documentation, algorithms, and binaries provided by the Licensor, including but not limited to the AST Parser Engines, Transformation Operator Algebra, Dependency Graph Engine, Conflict Tensor Engine, and PR Collision Radar components.

1.2. "Active Contributor" means an individual human author who has authored at least one (1) commit across any and all repositories registered with, monitored by, or analyzed by the Software during the preceding ninety (90) rolling calendar days, determined by unique Git author email address. Automated bot accounts (e.g., dependabot, renovate, github-actions[bot]) and pure automated merge commits are excluded.

1.3. "Production Use" means any deployment or execution of the Software in an automated continuous integration (CI/CD) pipeline, automated pull request review system, shared server infrastructure, or commercial environment for the operational benefit of an entity. Local developer sandboxes, educational learning, and temporary evaluation environments do not constitute Production Use.

1.4. "Modification" means any change, addition, deletion, patch, derivative work, or adaptation to the Software or its constituent modules.

1.5. "Competitive Service" means any service, platform, or commercial offering that provides pull request collision detection, semantic code conflict analysis, or merge intelligence substantially similar to the Software to third parties on a hosted, managed, multi-tenant, or API-accessible basis.

1.6. "Licensor" means Sarthak Basnet.

