## 3. Permitted Production Use ("Community Safe Harbor")

You are granted a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to make Production Use of the Software for internal repository auditing, provided that you satisfy ALL of the following conditions:

3.1. Scale Limitation: The total aggregated number of Active Contributors across all repositories analyzed by the Software within your organization does not exceed twenty (20) individuals. Organizations may not circumvent this limit by deploying multiple isolated instances.

3.2. Non-Competitive Limitation: The Software is not used to operate, power, or support a Competitive Service.

3.3. Attribution: All copies, distributions, and substantial portions of the Software must retain this License and all original copyright, author, and trademark notices.

Any Production Use exceeding twenty (20) Active Contributors requires a separate written Commercial Agreement from the Licensor.

---

## 4. Mandatory Reciprocal Share-Back for Modifications

If you create, compile, or execute any Modification of the Software and deploy such Modification for Production Use (whether externally distributed or executed exclusively within your private organization and network), you must satisfy one of the following obligations within thirty (30) calendar days of initial production deployment:

4.1. Public Publication: Make the complete corresponding source code of the Modification publicly available under the terms of this License in a prominent, freely accessible Git repository; OR

4.2. Secure Upstream Submission: Submit the complete source code of the Modification directly to the Licensor via private electronic transmission. By submitting under this section, you grant the Licensor a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free, transferable, and sublicensable license to use, adapt, incorporate, and distribute the Modification in official GDSS releases, while retaining ownership of your contribution.

4.3. Private Modification Waiver: Organizations wishing to deploy Modifications for Production Use while keeping such Modifications confidential and proprietary must purchase an explicit Enterprise License with a Private Modification Waiver from the Licensor.

4.4. Scope Limitation: This Section 4 applies strictly to Modifications of the Software. It does not apply to unmodified official releases, nor does it require disclosure of unrelated proprietary source code, secrets, credentials, or independent third-party software communicating with the Software via standard CLI, MCP, or JSON-RPC interfaces.

